invariant: INV-14
file: srv_flight.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: the binder is checked against the hash of the whole ClientHello, binders
  included, where RFC 9846 §4.3.11.2 computes it over the hello truncated
  before the binders list (rfc9846.txt:2591-2598). No client can produce a
  binder over bytes that contain it, so every resumption fails with
  decrypt_error. test/srv_resume_tests.h reads back binder_hash for a hello
  truncated at a known point.

--- old
        sha256_update(&partial, raw, 4 + ch->truncated_len);
--- new
        sha256_update(&partial, raw, raw_len);
